    <item>
      <title>Future Media Computing Lab Officially Established</title>
      <link>https://zhaoqma.github.io/post/20-12-02-icml-best-paper/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 15 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://zhaoqma.github.io/post/20-12-02-icml-best-paper/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Congratulations on the official establishment of the Future Media Computing Lab! We look forward to the lab making groundbreaking contributions to the field of AI and intelligent media computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are pleased to announce the official establishment of the Future Media Computing Lab (FMCL), a cutting-edge research lab under the School of Information Science and Technology at the University of Science and Technology of China. The lab is led by Professor Xiaojun Chang, a globally recognized expert in multimedia understanding and artificial intelligence, with Professor Xun Yang serving as the deputy director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Future Media Computing Lab is committed to advancing the frontiers of AI-driven media computing, with a focus on intelligent content analysis, generation, interaction, and transmission. The lab aims to bridge the gap between human cognition and machine perception, driving innovation in both theoretical foundations and real-world applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The lab currently hosts a diverse group of Ph.D. students, master’s candidates, and postdoctoral researchers, with close collaborations across institutions and international universities. FMCL fosters an open, inclusive, and innovative research environment, welcoming students and scholars with a passion for shaping the future of intelligent media.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We actively seek academic partnerships, industry collaborations, and talented researchers. If you are interested in joining us or working together on exciting problems at the intersection of AI and media, please reach out via our official website or contact us directly at [email address].&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    
